items.test:
New apps/mobile/src/screens/replay/__tests__/replayLargeText.test.tsx renders a bot-practice replay at font scale 2 and at 1. It checks:
- every Text or TextInput on both cards is capped ≤ ×1.35, with the flag and the bot chip at ×1.0;
- 'חושב' is at ×1.35;
- the score row height equals compactRows, and the margins leave the TextInput at least its box + 1;
- the activity row has minHeight and no fixed height;
- the card has minHeight 160 and no fixed height;
- the header subtitle has no numberOfLines;
- the compactRows values are right, and a no-strip card fits 160 at the cap.
It fails on the old code (no compactRows; activity and flag uncapped; subtitle numberOfLines 1). Existing player, replay, game (GroupHud), results, levels and dev-section tests pass.

items.rootCause:
explain.ts passed the digit list of naked.missing and naked.seen as one string, with no count. So every language had a single form. Arabic always said 'الأرقام' with a plural verb, even for one digit ('توجد بالفعل الأرقام 6'). Other languages were affected too:
- Polish 'są już:' is a plural verb;
- Turkish 'şunlar var:' is a plural pronoun;
- es, fr, it, pt-BR and de miss the article for a single digit;
- Spanish/Portuguese 'faltan/faltam' is plural.
Arabic hiddenPair said 'للأرقام' (plural) for exactly two digits.

